  "text": "The upsides first: plain loin is a world away from processed pork. It does not need curing, smoking, breading, or a mystery ingredient list to work. One roast can cover several meals. Dinner first, then sandwiches, wraps, or stir-fries with the leftovers. The mild flavour takes seasoning really well. Change the herbs, spice mix, or sauce and the same cut can go in a completely different direction.",
